# Default company data shown on the cotizador's "Datos de la Empresa" tab until the
# user edits it there (after which it lives in localStorage, not here). These are
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars, so Next.js inlines them into the client bundle at build time —
# they're readable in the browser, same as the hardcoded values they replaced. Moving
# them here only keeps real bank/personal data out of the git repo and lets it differ
# per Vercel environment (Production / Preview / Development).
#
# Set the real values in Vercel: Project Settings -> Environment Variables. For local
# dev, copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in test values.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPANY_NOMBRE=
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPANY_NIT=
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPANY_DIRECCION=
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPANY_CIUDAD=
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPANY_TELEFONOS=
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPANY_EMAIL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPANY_REPRESENTANTE=
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPANY_CEDULA=
NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPANY_DATOS_BANCARIOS=
